1) Creating a Laravel Project


composer create-project laravel/laravel:^12.0 task-manager

We used ^12.0 becuase the latest laravel version would have got installed which requires the php verion 8.3+ 


2) In the project directory run the php artisan list command to list all the artisan commands and its use.	


What is Artisan -  you are running Laravel's command-line interface (CLI). 

the basic syntax php artisan COMMAND [OPTIONS] [ARGUMENTS]


1) Migrations -

to make migrations use: make command

php artisan migration:status to which migration has run and which are pending

php artisan make:migrations filename
eg php artisan make:migrations create_state_master_table  this will creat the table name state_master

php artisan migrate to run the database migrations for all the tables.

for single table use path + migration file name with extension
php artisan migrate --path-/database/migrations/migrationfilename.php
php artisan migrate --path=/database/migrations/2026_09_24_062404_create_state_master_table.php


once the migration has run and the is no longer pending i.e the table has been created you cannot change the migration file if you for example add unique constraint or add a new column in creatin table after the migration was run

then you have to create new migration

using - php artisan make:migration add_department_id_to_employee_table
another eg - php artisan make:migration add_unique_constraint_to_department_name_to_department_master_table

php artisan migrate:rollback to reverse the migrations according to the down method of each migration table/file.


check the pendig migration :  php artisan migrate:status which are not run/are not in the database migrationstable.

