Equolent Model commands and their use - Php artisan tinker for learing Equolent commands

Php artisan tinker 

1) ::create   - This command is used to create one Eloquent record

For eg  with model related to a database 

App\Models\Employee::create(['fullname'=>'test',''=>'email'=>'test@gmail.com','address'=>'add line 1','citystatemap_id'=>'1', 'phone_no'=>'7845754854'],);

you can create record for that table directly through command line.

2) ::insert - This command is used for creating multiple records unlike create which only allows you to create a single record.

App\Models\CityMaster::create([ (['city_name'='Mumbai']), (['city_name'='Pune']), (['city_name'='Kolkata']), (['city_name'='Noida']),]);

3)  :: all - This command is used for finding all the records in the table/model
App\Models\DepartmentMaster::all;
Give me a collection containing all departments.
select * from department

4) ::find - This command is used to find the record using the primary key column and finds the exact primary key id that we passed
App\Models\DepartmentMaster::find(2);
Find the DepartmentMaster whose primary key is 2 if the id=2 not exist it will return null.
Select id from department_master where id=2 limit 1; 

4) ::findorfail(1) - This command is used for finding the primary key value from the model/table but while the find returns null if not found findorfail returns ModelNotFoundException error.
App\Models\DepartmentMaster::findorfail(2);
Find the DepartmentMaster whose primary key is 2 if id=2 not exist it will return ModelNotFoundException error
Select id from department_master where id=2 limit 1; 

5) ::where - Used query using the where condition

App\Models\DepartmentMaster::where('department_name','Human Resource')->get();
select * from department where department_name='Human Resource'  also ->get is used to run the query

App\Models\DepartmentMaster::wherein('department_name',['Human Resource','UI UX','IT'])->get();
select * from department where department_name='Human Resource'

App\Models\DepartmentMaster::where('department_name', 'like', 'Hum%' )->get(); 
select * from department where department_name='Human Resource'


App\Models\DepartmentMaster::where('department_name', '!=', ' ')->get();
select * from department where department_name!=' ';

App\Models\DepartmentMaster::where('created_at', '>=', '2026-09-25')->get();
select * from department where created_at >= '2026-09-25';

App\Models\DepartmentMaster::whereNotNull('department_name')
    ->where('created_at', '<=', '2026-09-25')
    ->get();


6) get() vs first()  - get will execute your query and return all records but first will only return the first record for eg

App\Models\DepartmentMaster::where('department_name', 'like', 'I%' )->get();
This will return all the records.
select * from department_master where department_name like 'I%'

App\Models\DepartmentMaster::where('department_name', 'like', 'I%' )->first();
This will return only first matching record.
select * from department_master where department_name like 'I%' limit 1

7) ::whereNotNull -
$departments = App\Models\DepartmentMaster::whereNotNull('department_name')->get();

